---
description: FlowCRM project development rules
alwaysApply: true
---

- Read docs/PROJECT_PLAN.md before making architectural changes.
- Use Java 21 and Spring Boot for the backend.
- Use React, TypeScript and Vite for the frontend when UI work is in scope.
- Follow controller-service-repository layering.
- Use DTOs for API requests and responses.
- Never expose JPA entities directly from controllers.
- Validate all user input.
- Use Flyway migrations rather than Hibernate schema generation.
- Database schema changes must use new Flyway migrations.
- Never hardcode secrets, database passwords, JWT keys, or infrastructure credentials.
- Keep secrets and infrastructure configuration externalized through environment variables.
- Do not add infrastructure patterns merely for appearance; use them only in the planned locations in docs/PROJECT_PLAN.md.
- Preserve transactional integrity between business writes and outbox writes.
- Consumers must tolerate duplicate message delivery.
- Do not implement asynchronous side effects directly inside HTTP controllers.
- Add tests for failure, retry, and idempotency behavior when those features are implemented.
- Do not delete or rewrite existing working functionality without explaining why.
- Implement one feature at a time.
- Run relevant tests after each implementation.
- Before modifying more than five files, describe the planned changes.
- Do not commit or push unless explicitly instructed.
